  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nShortwave across west central MO as of 18Z is expected to work east \nthis afternoon and evening allowing upper level ridge across the \nsouthwestern US to expand north and east. Upper level subsidence \nbehind departing shortwave should lead to a reduction in storm \npotential late this afternoon into this evening, but CAMs have \noffered a variety of solutions of isolated shower/storm activity, \nlargely focused south of I-70 through the evening hours.  Moist \nadiabatic lapse rates aloft keep instability limited, but partial \nclearing across eastern KS into west central Missouri may allow for \na late afternoon/evening pop up storm.  Weak shear should keep \nanything that develops subsevere.  \n\nWeak low level jet is expected build heat and humidity northward \ntonight strengthening capping inversion across the region and \ntemperatures remaining in the 70s overnight. Heat is expected to \nbuild further on Saturday, and have issued a heat advisory along and \nsouth of I-70 Saturday. Heat is expected to build further Sunday \ninto Monday, and have issued a heat advisory area wide through \nMonday evening. Models suggest there may be a few ridge ridging \nshort waves, one that may result in an MCS Sunday night into Monday \nmorning across the Upper Midwest. Through collaboration, have sided \nwith the idea that there will be limiting lingering impacts across \nthe region on Monday.\n\nA cold front may try to build south across the region Monday night \ninto Tuesday.  South of the front, there is the potential for the \nneed for additional heat headlines, but the timing of the front is \nunclear at this point. \n\nLongwave pattern remains late into the week with upper ridge across \nthe western CONUS, with shortwaves continuing along the northern \nperiphery of the ridge.  With little agreement on timing of the \nwaves, left the model blend as is with above normal temperatures \nand periodic low chances of precipitation.",
